{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T09:54:56.096Z","ordinal":67822,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a115c9-99e0-7b00-a829-209d6cd1dd7b","call_id":"call_49595b361d52417881a56e890fcd3208","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__linear_get_issue\",\"description\":\"Plan and build products\\n\\nRetrieve detailed information about an issue by ID, including attachments, git branch name, and active Triage Intelligence suggestions when the issue is in triage. This tool is part of plugin `Linear`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linear_get_issue(args: {\\n  // Issue ID or identifier (e.g., LIN-123)\\n  id: string;\\n  // Include associated customer needs\\n  includeCustomerNeeds?: boolean;\\n  // Include blocking/related/duplicate relations\\n  includeRelations?: boolean;\\n  // Include associated releases\\n  includeReleases?: boolean;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__linear_list_comments\",\"description\":\"Plan and build products\\n\\nList comments on a Linear issue, project, initiative, document, project milestone, or project/initiative status update. Provide exactly one of `issueId`, `projectId`, `initiativeId`, `documentId`, `milestoneId`, or `statusUpdateId`. For issues, projects, and initiatives this returns both top-level discussion threads and inline description comments. Inline (anchored) comments carry a non-null `quotedText` set to the snippet of description text they reference. Returned comments include `author` and nullable `onBehalfOf`; when set, `onBehalfOf` identifies the user the agent author acted for. This tool is part of plugin `Linear`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linear_list_comments(args: {\\n  // Next page cursor\\n  cursor?: string;\\n  // Document ID or slug (provide exactly one parent)\\n  documentId?: string;\\n  // Initiative name, ID, identifier (e.g., INIT-123), or slug (provide exactly one parent)\\n  initiativeId?: string;\\n  // Issue ID or identifier (e.g., LIN-123) (provide exactly one parent)\\n  issueId?: string;\\n  // Max results (default 50, max 250)\\n  limit?: number;\\n  // Milestone UUID (provide exactly one parent). Resolve milestone names via `list_milestones` first.\\n  milestoneId?: string;\\n  // Sort: createdAt | updatedAt\\n  orderBy?: \\\"createdAt\\\" | \\\"updatedAt\\\";\\n  // Project name, ID, identifier (e.g., PROJ-123), or slug (provide exactly one parent)\\n  projectId?: string;\\n  // Status update UUID (provide exactly one parent). Resolve status updates via `get_status_updates` first.\\n  statusUpdateId?: string;\\n  // Type of status update named by `statusUpdateId`, as returned by `get_status_updates`. Only valid together with `statusUpdateId`; omit to check both project and initiative status updates.\\n  statusUpdateType?: \\\"project\\\" | \\\"initiative\\\";\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__linear_get_status_updates\",\"description\":\"Plan and build products\\n\\nList or get project/initiative status updates. Pass `id` to get a specific update, or filter to list. This tool is part of plugin `Linear`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linear_get_status_updates(args: {\\n  // Created after: ISO-8601 date/duration (e.g., -P1D)\\n  createdAt?: string;\\n  // Next page cursor\\n  cursor?: string;\\n  // Status update ID - if provided, returns this specific update\\n  id?: string;\\n  // Include archived items\\n  includeArchived?: boolean;\\n  // Initiative name, ID, identifier (e.g., INIT-123), or slug\\n  initiative?: string;\\n  // Max results (default 50, max 250)\\n  limit?: number;\\n  // Sort: createdAt | updatedAt\\n  orderBy?: \\\"createdAt\\\" | \\\"updatedAt\\\";\\n  // Project name, ID, identifier (e.g., PROJ-123), or slug\\n  project?: string;\\n  // Type of status update\\n  type: \\\"project\\\" | \\\"initiative\\\";\\n  // Updated after: ISO-8601 date/duration (e.g., -P1D)\\n  updatedAt?: string;\\n  // User ID, name, email, or \\\"me\\\"\\n  user?: string;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__linear_save_issue\",\"description\":\"Plan and build products\\n\\nCreate or update a Linear issue. If `id` is provided, updates the existing issue; otherwise creates a new one. When creating, `team` is required, and `title` is required unless `template` is set. Note: use `assignee` (not `assigneeId`) to set the assignee — it accepts a user ID, name, email, or \\\"me\\\". This tool is part of plugin `Linear`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linear_save_issue(args: { addLabels?: Array<string>; addReleases?: Array<string>; assignee?: string | null; blockedBy?: Array<string>; blocks?: Array<string>; cycle?: string | null; delegate?: string | null; description?: string; dueDate?: string | null; duplicateOf?: string | null; estimate?: number | null; id?: string; labels?: Array<string>; links?: Array<{ title: string; url: string; }>; milestone?: string; parentId?: string | null; patch?: Array<{ new_string: string; old_string: string; op: \\\"replace\\\"; replace_all?: boolean; } | { anchor: string; op: \\\"insert_before\\\"; text: string; } | { anchor: string; op: \\\"insert_after\\\"; text: string; } | { op: \\\"prepend\\\"; text: string; } | { op: \\\"append\\\"; text: string; } | { from: string; new_string: string; op: \\\"replace_range\\\"; to: string; }>; priority?: number; project?: string | null; relatedTo?: Array<string>; removeBlockedBy?: Array<string>; removeBlocks?: Array<string>; removeLabels?: Array<string>; removeRelatedTo?: Array<string>; removeReleases?: Array<string>; setReleases?: Array<string>; slaBreachesAt?: string | null; slaType?: \\\"all\\\" | \\\"onlyBusinessDays\\\" | null; state?: string; team?: string; template?: string; title?: string; }): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__linear_save_comment\",\"description\":\"Plan and build products\\n\\nCreate or update a comment on a Linear issue, project, initiative, document, project milestone, or project/initiative status update. If `id` is provided, updates the existing comment; otherwise creates a new one. To start a new thread, pass `body` and exactly one of `issueId`, `projectId`, `initiativeId`, `documentId`, `milestoneId`, or `statusUpdateId` — comments on issues/projects/initiatives become top-level discussion threads; comments on documents/milestones become description comments. A status update holds a single thread, so a comment on an update that already has one is added to it as a reply. To reply to an existing thread, pass `parentId` and `body`; the reply inherits the parent's thread type, so no entity reference is needed. Parent reference fields are ignored when `id` or `parentId` is provided (`statusUpdateType` is rejected instead). This tool is part of plugin `Linear`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linear_save_comment(args: {\\n  // Content as Markdown. Do not escape the string — use literal newlines and special characters, not escape sequences. To mention a user, use @displayName (e.g., @johndoe)\\n  body: string;\\n  // Document ID or slug (provide exactly one parent)\\n  documentId?: string;\\n  // Comment ID. If provided, updates the existing comment\\n  id?: string;\\n  // Initiative name, ID, identifier (e.g., INIT-123), or slug (provide exactly one parent)\\n  initiativeId?: string;\\n  // Issue ID or identifier (e.g., LIN-123) (provide exactly one parent)\\n  issueId?: string;\\n  // Milestone UUID (provide exactly one parent). Resolve milestone names via `list_milestones` first.\\n  milestoneId?: string;\\n  // Parent comment ID (for replies, only when creating)\\n  parentId?: string;\\n  // Project name, ID, identifier (e.g., PROJ-123), or slug (provide exactly one parent)\\n  projectId?: string;\\n  // Status update UUID (provide exactly one parent). Resolve status updates via `get_status_updates` first.\\n  statusUpdateId?: string;\\n  // Type of status update named by `statusUpdateId`, as returned by `get_status_updates`. Only valid together with `statusUpdateId`; omit to check both project and initiative status updates.\\n  statusUpdateType?: \\\"project\\\" | \\\"initiative\\\";\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__linear_save_status_update\",\"description\":\"Plan and build products\\n\\nCreate or update a project/initiative status update. Omit `id` to create, provide `id` to update. This tool is part of plugin `Linear`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linear_save_status_update(args: {\\n  // Content as Markdown. Do not escape the string — use literal newlines and special characters, not escape sequences. To mention a user, use @displayName (e.g., @johndoe)\\n  body?: string;\\n  // onTrack | atRisk | offTrack\\n  health?: \\\"onTrack\\\" | \\\"atRisk\\\" | \\\"offTrack\\\";\\n  // Status update ID - if provided, updates this existing update\\n  id?: string;\\n  // Initiative name, ID, identifier (e.g., INIT-123), or slug\\n  initiative?: string;\\n  // Deprecated. Hide diff with previous update (create only)\\n  isDiffHidden?: boolean;\\n  // Project name, ID, identifier (e.g., PROJ-123), or slug\\n  project?: string;\\n  // Type of status update\\n  type: \\\"project\\\" | \\\"initiative\\\";\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"d7bd60\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000005625,\"exit_code\":1,\"original_token_count\":1138,\"output\":\"    };\\n    PostHog.proto