{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T09:58:56.485Z","ordinal":67899,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac617deb38887d0933b4addf245f2c4","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I’m using the repository’s package and Effect client skills for the analytics work. They help keep the shared event rules in one place and keep browser code separate from private management keys. The local handover check is still running; no PostHog project or credential has been changed."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1791367134723,"completed_at_ms":1791367136485}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T09:58:56.487Z","ordinal":67900,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac617deb38887d0933b4addf245f2c4","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"I’m using the repository’s package and Effect client skills for the analytics work. They help keep the shared event rules in one place and keep browser code separate from private management keys. The local handover check is still running; no PostHog project or credential has been changed."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","create_time":1791367134.7074337,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac617deb38887d0933b4addf245f2c4","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a115cd-44e7-7812-81e5-0b24393e28c4","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":1434}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T09:58:59.475Z","ordinal":67901,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac617e072a887d0b7f1bbab6f27b424","status":"completed","call_id":"call_ce96da12172242809447026a45d69884","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat .agents/skills/package-structure/references/repository-profile.md && sed -n '1,180p' .agents/skills/package-structure/references/package-contract.md && sed -n '1,135p' .agents/skills/package-structure/references/renderer-and-safety.md && rg -n '^export .*layer|^export' node_modules/effect/src/Crypto.ts | tail -12 && rg --files node_modules/effect/src | rg 'Crypto' && cat packages/api/rpc/package.json && tail -14 /private/tmp/dev78-handover-whole-b-verification.log\",max_output_tokens:4300}));\ntext(await tools.clock__curr_time({}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","create_time":1791367136.4530118}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T09:58:59.586Z","ordinal":67902,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5a7afee8-6bed-4c48-8251-f3150d5a8840","process_id":"22476","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat .agents/skills/package-structure/references/repository-profile.md && sed -n '1,180p' .agents/skills/package-structure/references/package-contract.md && sed -n '1,135p' .agents/skills/package-structure/references/renderer-and-safety.md && rg -n '^export .*layer|^export' node_modules/effect/src/Crypto.ts | tail -12 && rg --files node_modules/effect/src | rg 'Crypto' && cat packages/api/rpc/package.json && tail -14 /private/tmp/dev78-handover-whole-b-verification.log"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"cat .agents/skills/package-structure/references/repository-profile.md && sed -n '1,180p' .agents/skills/package-structure/references/package-contract.md && sed -n '1,135p' .agents/skills/package-structure/references/renderer-and-safety.md && rg -n '^export .*layer|^export' node_modules/effect/src/Crypto.ts | tail -12 && rg --files node_modules/effect/src | rg 'Crypto' && cat packages/api/rpc/package.json && tail -14 /private/tmp/dev78-handover-whole-b-verification.log"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# TaxKit package profile\n\n- Repository root: current checkout resolved with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`\n- Package manager/workspaces: Bun with the root's nested workspace globs\n- Namespace: `@taxkit/*`\n- Source condition: `source`\n- Default internal build: `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json`\n- Exceptions: `@taxkit/docs-content` and private `@taxkit/infrastructure` are source-only; `@taxkit/docs-fumadocs` is private compiled; the TypeScript SDK is publishable/dist-only and requires clean publish exports, packed-artifact, and downstream-consumer proof\n- Changesets and production Knip are part of release-facing package changes\n- Verification: focused package commands, `bun run test:skills`, and `bun run verification`; for release-facing work run `bun run release:check` (including SDK packed/downstream checks)\n- Architecture routes: `docs/architecture/package-ownership.md`, `docs/architecture/package-boundaries.md`, `docs/architecture/effect-services.md`, and `docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md`\n- Preserve unrelated work; never overwrite it.\n\n## Clean-slate compatibility and implementation\n\nThe local root manifest and lockfile select stable Effect 4.0.0 and TypeScript\n7.0.2. Canonical skill templates may retain their upstream rc.117 qualification;\nthat reference snapshot does not downgrade TaxKit or prove an app/provider\nmigration. Check installed exports and the active clean-slate plan before use.\n\nThe complete local skill collection is pinned by\n`tools/skills/canonical-skill-baseline.json` to Commonplace development-workflows\n0.6.1. It includes `linear`, `strict-effect-ts` and `alchemy-iac`, with relative\nClaude links. Use the Linear skill for tracked task status/evidence. The active\n`docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md` distinguishes skill adoption, strict enforcement and Atom integration from\nlater application work. Use its task receipts for current acceptance; the\nupstream skill receipt alone does not prove runtime behaviour.\n# Package contract\n\n## Ownership before files\n\nName the capability, its callers, its untrusted boundaries, its runtime owner,\nand why an existing package cannot own it. A package is justified by a stable\nsemantic boundary, not by file count.\n\nCompiled packages use `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json`, relative internal imports\nwith explicit `.js` endings, and explicit exports. Use the same endings in\ntests; TypeScript and the source consumer resolve them to the matching `.ts`\nfiles, while ordinary ESM consumers load the emitted `.js` files. Root exports\nare absent by default; an intentional root\nmust remain contract-only. The source condition maps to `src`, `types` to\ndeclarations, and `default` to `dist`. `publishConfig.exports` omits the source\ncondition. Source-only packages point both development/default resolution at\nsource and explain the bundler requirement in their package README.\n\nRequired Effect service paths:\n\n```text\nsrc/schemas.ts\nsrc/errors.ts\nsrc/service.ts\nsrc/live.layer.ts\nsrc/test.layer.ts\nsrc/__testing__/fixtures.ts\nsrc/__testing__/observations.ts\ntest/service.test.ts\n```\n\nUse `mock.layer.ts` only when its semantics are distinct from the deterministic\ntest Layer. Tests live under `test/`; `src/__testing__` contains reusable setup,\nfixtures, and observations only.\n\nEach package README names the semantic owner, public/live/test export paths,\ndownstream architecture/proof impact, runbook applicability, and explicit\nnon-claims. Repository profiles—not this global contract—name exact local\ncommands and document paths.\n\n## Separate source, domain and transport owners\n\nAuthored content may live in a source-only package. It exports files and source\ninventory; the domain package owns the validation Schemas and source loader,\nservice, named errors and live/test Layers. Apps supply bundler/host adapters.\nDo not give the source package another runtime or duplicate domain definitions.\nHTTP, RPC and MCP reuse explicit domain exports. Client exports must resolve\nwithout importing handlers, the live source loader, renderer or MCP server.\nCheck the actual browser bundle as well as the export map.\n\n## Export proof\n\nConsumer fixtures must prove all four modes:\n\n1. repository source condition resolves source;\n2. TypeScript resolves emitted declarations;\n3. default resolution uses built JavaScript;\n4. packed/publish exports omit source-only paths and conditions.\n\nNever rely only on checking that export keys exist.\n\n`publishConfig.exports` is not a portable manifest rewrite: npm and Bun pack may\nretain the development `exports` map, while other package managers may apply the\npublish map. A publishable package therefore needs the repository's explicit\nstaged-manifest/prepack path and tarball inspection. Prove the actual publisher\nused by that repository; do not infer a clean tarball from `publishConfig`.\n# Renderer and safety\n\n`render_package.py` accepts a kind, an absolute new target, a valid scoped\npackage name, a source condition, a JSON version snapshot, and—when needed—an\nexisting domain package name.\n\nIt refuses relative paths, lexical traversal, filesystem/home/repository roots,\nexisting targets, symlinked parents/assets, invalid names, and missing aligned\nEffect v4 versions. It renders in a sibling staging directory, validates, writes\n`package-structure.render.json`, then atomically renames. Failure removes the\nstaging directory. There is no force option.\n\nThe source condition must be a custom name such as `@scope/source`, not an\nempty, malformed or standard condition such as `types`, `default` or `node`.\nEvery compiled export keeps that recorded condition first and points it at an\nexisting source file. Repository and package receipts must agree on the name.\n\nThe version snapshot must contain an ISO date and an exact `effect` version.\nTemplates target DAW's qualified Effect `4.0.0-rc.117` API, including\n`Schema.TaggedError`. The renderer accepts current v4 RC/stable snapshots and\nhas no legacy API switch. A different selected release needs qualification of\nthe canonical templates before adoption.\nNetwork resolution belongs to repository snapshot maintenance, never rendering.\nThe render manifest records the snapshot date and content digest, never the\nabsolute installation or source path.\n\nUse an isolated temporary directory for smoke tests. Do not point the renderer\nat a dirty live package; audit and patch that package deliberately instead.\n40:export type DigestAlgorithm = \"SHA-1\" | \"SHA-256\" | \"SHA-384\" | \"SHA-512\"\n78:export interface Crypto {\n191:export const Crypto: Context.Service<Crypto, Crypto> = Context.Service(\"effect/Crypto\")\n230:export const make = (\nnode_modules/effect/src/Crypto.ts\n{\n  \"name\": \"@taxkit/api-rpc\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"exports\": {\n    \"./group\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/group.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/group.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/group.js\"\n    },\n    \"./handlers\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/handlers.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/handlers.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/handlers.js\"\n    },\n    \"./service\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/service.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/service.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/service.js\"\n    },\n    \"./server\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/server.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/server.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/server.js\"\n    },\n    \"./live\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/live.layer.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/live.layer.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/live.layer.js\"\n    },\n    \"./test\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/test.layer.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/test.layer.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/test.layer.js\"\n    },\n    \"./schemas\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/schemas.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/schemas.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/schemas.js\"\n    },\n    \"./errors\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/errors.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/errors.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/errors.js\"\n    },\n    \"./testing/fixtures\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/__testing__/fixtures.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/__testing__/fixtures.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/__testing__/fixtures.js\"\n    },\n    \"./request-boundary\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/request-boundary.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/request-boundary.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/request-boundary.js\"\n    },\n    \"./host-telemetry\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/host-telemetry.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/host-telemetry.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/host-telemetry.js\"\n    },\n    \"./rate-identity\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/rate-identity.boundary.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/rate-identity.boundary.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/rate-identity.boundary.js\"\n    },\n    \"./content/group\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/content.group.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/content.group.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/content.group.js\"\n    },\n    \"./content/handlers\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/content.handlers.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/content.handlers.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/content.handlers.js\"\n    },\n    \"./content/schemas\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/content.schemas.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/content.schemas.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/content.schemas.js\"\n    },\n    \"./content/errors\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/content.errors.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/content.errors.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/content.errors.js\"\n    },\n    \"./content/service\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/content.service.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/content.service.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/content.service.js\"\n    },\n    \"./content/live\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/content.live.layer.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/content.live.layer.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/content.live.layer.js\"\n    },\n    \"./content/test\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/content.test.layer.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/content.test.layer.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/content.test.layer.js\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"publishConfig\": {\n    \"exports\": {\n      \"./group\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/group.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/group.js\"\n      },\n      \"./service\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/service.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/service.js\"\n      },\n      \"./server\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/server.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/server.js\"\n      },\n      \"./live\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/live.layer.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/live.layer.js\"\n      },\n      \"./content/group\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/content.group.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/content.group.js\"\n      },\n      \"./content/service\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/content.service.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/content.service.js\"\n      },\n      \"./content/live\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/content.live.layer.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/content.live.layer.js\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"rm -rf dist && tsc -p tsconfig.build.json\",\n    \"check-types\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"test\": \"bun --bun vitest run\",\n    \"clean\": \"rm -rf dist .turbo *.tsbuildinfo\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@taxkit/api-http\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/calculators\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/content\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"effect\": \"catalog:\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@effect/vitest\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"@taxkit/core\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/rules-au-pay\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"typescript\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vite\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vitest\": \"catalog:\"\n  }\n}\n   Duration  640ms (tests 68%, import 25%, transform 6%, worker 1%)\n\n$ turbo run //#test:quality-workflow:task\n\n   • turbo 2.11.7\n   • Packages in scope: //\n   • Running //#test:quality-workflow:task in 1 package\n   • Remote caching disabled, using shared worktree cache\n\n//:test:quality-workflow:task: cache miss, executing e7830848b768980d\n//:test:quality-workflow:task: $ bun --bun vitest run --config tools/vitest.config.ts tools/quality-workflow\n//:test:quality-workflow:task: \n//:test:quality-workflow:task:  RUN  v5.0.3 /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit\n//:test:quality-workflow:task: \n","